<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Portara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 530 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Portara is a massive marble doorway on the islet of Palatia at the harbour of Naxos town, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, the only standing part of an unfinished temple begun around 530 BCE under the tyrant Lygdamis. The temple, probably dedicated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a>, was abandoned after Lygdamis fell. Some 6 metres high, the gateway has become the emblem of Naxos.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/portara.jpg" alt="Portara" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean Housen · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20221029_Naxos_762.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
